<h2 data-start=3D"3263" data-end=3D"3282" class=3D"">3. Encapsulation</h2>
<p data-start=3D"3284" data-end=3D"3501" class=3D"">L=E2=80=99<strong data-=
start=3D"3286" data-end=3D"3303">encapsulation</strong> est un principe cl=
=C3=A9 de la POO. Elle consiste =C3=A0 cacher les d=C3=A9tails internes d=
=E2=80=99une classe et =C3=A0 n=E2=80=99exposer que les informations n=C3=
=A9cessaires. En PHP, cela se fait =C3=A0 l=E2=80=99aide des <strong data-s=
tart=3D"3475" data-end=3D"3500">modificateurs d'acc=C3=A8s</strong>.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3503" data-end=3D"3759">
<li data-start=3D"3503" data-end=3D"3606" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3505" data-end=3D"3606" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
505" data-end=3D"3515">public</strong> : Acc=C3=A8de =C3=A0 la propri=C3=A9=
t=C3=A9 ou m=C3=A9thode de partout (y compris depuis l'ext=C3=A9rieur de la=
 classe).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3607" data-end=3D"3671" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3609" data-end=3D"3671" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
609" data-end=3D"3620">private</strong> : Ne permet l=E2=80=99acc=C3=A8s qu=
=E2=80=99=C3=A0 l=E2=80=99int=C3=A9rieur de la classe.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3672" data-end=3D"3759" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3674" data-end=3D"3759" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
674" data-end=3D"3687">protected</strong> : Permet l'acc=C3=A8s uniquement =
=C3=A0 la classe et aux classes qui en h=C3=A9ritent.</p>
</li>
</ul>
