<p data-start=3D"3938" data-end=3D"3956" class=3D"">Dans cet exemple :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3957" data-end=3D"4190">
<li data-start=3D"3957" data-end=3D"3986" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3959" data-end=3D"3986" class=3D"">Le cookie s'appelle <co=
de data-start=3D"3979" data-end=3D"3985">user</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3987" data-end=3D"4025" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3989" data-end=3D"4025" class=3D"">La valeur du cookie est=
 <code data-start=3D"4013" data-end=3D"4024">"JohnDoe"</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4026" data-end=3D"4111" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4028" data-end=3D"4111" class=3D"">Le cookie expirera dans=
 30 jours (30 jours * 24 heures * 60 minutes * 60 secondes).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4112" data-end=3D"4190" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4114" data-end=3D"4190" class=3D"">Le cookie sera accessib=
le sur toute la dur=C3=A9e du domaine (indiqu=C3=A9 par <code data-start=3D=
"4183" data-end=3D"4188">"/"</code>).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"4192" data-end=3D"4195" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"4197" data-end=3D"4222" class=3D"">3. Lecture des Cookies=
</h2>
<p data-start=3D"4224" data-end=3D"4438" class=3D"">Une fois qu'un cookie a=
 =C3=A9t=C3=A9 cr=C3=A9=C3=A9 et envoy=C3=A9 au navigateur de l'utilisateur=
, il peut =C3=AAtre r=C3=A9cup=C3=A9r=C3=A9 via la superglobale <code data-=
start=3D"4341" data-end=3D"4351">$_COOKIE</code> en PHP. Les cookies sont a=
ccessibles dans <code data-start=3D"4394" data-end=3D"4404">$_COOKIE</code>=
 sous forme de tableau associatif.</p>
