<hr data-start=3D"1344" data-end=3D"1347" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"1349" data-end=3D"1403" class=3D"">1. Introduction aux Ba=
ses de Donn=C3=A9es Relationnelles</h2>
<p data-start=3D"1405" data-end=3D"1777" class=3D"">Une base de donn=C3=A9e=
s relationnelle est une collection de donn=C3=A9es organis=C3=A9es de mani=
=C3=A8re structur=C3=A9e sous forme de tables, avec des relations entre ell=
es. Ces bases de donn=C3=A9es utilisent le mod=C3=A8le relationnel, o=C3=B9=
 les donn=C3=A9es sont stock=C3=A9es sous forme de lignes (enregistrements)=
 et de colonnes (attributs), et sont manipul=C3=A9es =C3=A0 l'aide du langa=
ge SQL (Structured Query Language).</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"1779" data-end=3D"1825" class=3D"">Exemple de gestion d'u=
ne base de donn=C3=A9es :</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1827" data-end=3D"2035" class=3D"">Imaginez une applicatio=
n de gestion de biblioth=C3=A8que. Vous aurez des informations sur les livr=
es, les emprunteurs et les emprunts. Ces informations peuvent =C3=AAtre org=
anis=C3=A9es dans diff=C3=A9rentes tables, telles que :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"2037" data-end=3D"2165">
<li data-start=3D"2037" data-end=3D"2069" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2039" data-end=3D"2069" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
039" data-end=3D"2049">Livres</strong> (id, titre, auteur)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2070" data-end=3D"2106" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2072" data-end=3D"2106" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
072" data-end=3D"2087">Emprunteurs</strong> (id, nom, adresse)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2107" data-end=3D"2165" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2109" data-end=3D"2165" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
109" data-end=3D"2121">Emprunts</strong> (id, id_emprunteur, id_livre, date=
_emprunt)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"2167" data-end=3D"2170" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"2172" data-end=3D"2196" class=3D"">2. Mod=C3=A8le Relatio=
nnel</h2>
<p data-start=3D"2198" data-end=3D"2389" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=
=3D"2201" data-end=3D"2223">mod=C3=A8le relationnel</strong> est bas=C3=A9 =
sur des tables, et les donn=C3=A9es dans une table sont organis=C3=A9es sou=
s forme de relations. Une relation entre deux tables est =C3=A9tablie par u=
ne <strong data-start=3D"2371" data-end=3D"2388">cl=C3=A9 =C3=A9trang=C3=A8=
re</strong>.</p>
<p data-start=3D"2391" data-end=3D"2439" class=3D"">Le mod=C3=A8le repose s=
ur trois concepts principaux :</p>
<ol data-start=3D"2440" data-end=3D"2701">
<li data-start=3D"2440" data-end=3D"2532" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2443" data-end=3D"2532" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
443" data-end=3D"2453">Entit=C3=A9</strong> : Repr=C3=A9sente un objet ou u=
ne chose (par exemple, un client, un produit, etc.).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2533" data-end=3D"2633" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2536" data-end=3D"2633" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
536" data-end=3D"2548">Attribut</strong> : Repr=C3=A9sente une propri=C3=A9=
t=C3=A9 d'une entit=C3=A9 (par exemple, un nom, une adresse, un prix).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2634" data-end=3D"2701" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2637" data-end=3D"2701" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
637" data-end=3D"2649">Relation</strong> : La fa=C3=A7on dont les entit=C3=
=A9s sont li=C3=A9es entre elles.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start=3D"2703" data-end=3D"2817" class=3D"">Chaque table repr=C3=A9=
sente une relation (ou entit=C3=A9) et chaque colonne de la table repr=C3=
=A9sente un attribut de l=E2=80=99entit=C3=A9.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2819" data-end=3D"2822" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"2824" data-end=3D"2856" class=3D"">3. Tables, Colonnes et=
 Lignes</h2>
<p data-start=3D"2858" data-end=3D"2945" class=3D"">Les donn=C3=A9es dans u=
ne base de donn=C3=A9es relationnelle sont organis=C3=A9es dans des <strong=
 data-start=3D"2934" data-end=3D"2944">tables</strong>.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"2947" data-end=3D"2974" class=3D"">Structure d=E2=80=99un=
e table :</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2976" data-end=3D"3430">
<li data-start=3D"2976" data-end=3D"3143" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2978" data-end=3D"3143" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
978" data-end=3D"2987">Table</strong> : C=E2=80=99est un ensemble de donn=
=C3=A9es structur=C3=A9es. Par exemple, une table appel=C3=A9e <code data-s=
tart=3D"3063" data-end=3D"3073">Employ=C3=A9s</code> pourrait contenir des =
informations sur les employ=C3=A9s d=E2=80=99une entreprise.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3144" data-end=3D"3281" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3146" data-end=3D"3281" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
146" data-end=3D"3158">Colonnes</strong> : Chaque table contient plusieurs =
colonnes, qui d=C3=A9finissent les types de donn=C3=A9es stock=C3=A9s (par =
exemple, nom, =C3=A2ge, salaire).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3282" data-end=3D"3430" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"3284" data-end=3D"3430" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"3=
284" data-end=3D"3294">Lignes</strong> : Les lignes repr=C3=A9sentent les e=
nregistrements individuels, chaque ligne contenant des valeurs pour les col=
onnes d=C3=A9finies dans la table.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"3432" data-end=3D"3446" class=3D"">Exemple :</h4>
<p data-start=3D"3448" data-end=3D"3466" class=3D"">Table <code data-start=
=3D"3454" data-end=3D"3464">Employ=C3=A9s</code> :</p>
<div class=3D"overflow-x-auto contain-inline-size"><table data-start=3D"346=
8" data-end=3D"3712" node=3D"[object Object]"><thead data-start=3D"3468" da=
ta-end=3D"3516"><tr data-start=3D"3468" data-end=3D"3516"><th data-start=3D=
"3468" data-end=3D"3481">id_employ=C3=A9</th><th data-start=3D"3481" data-e=
nd=3D"3493">nom</th><th data-start=3D"3493" data-end=3D"3505">poste</th><th=
 data-start=3D"3505" data-end=3D"3516">salaire</th></tr></thead><tbody data=
-start=3D"3566" data-end=3D"3712"><tr data-start=3D"3566" data-end=3D"3614"=
><td>1</td><td>Alice</td><td>Manager</td><td>50000</td></tr><tr data-start=
=3D"3615" data-end=3D"3663"><td>2</td><td>Bob</td><td>Developer</td><td>400=
00</td></tr><tr data-start=3D"3664" data-end=3D"3712"><td>3</td><td>Charlie=
</td><td>Designer</td><td>35000</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<hr data-start=3D"3714" data-end=3D"3717" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"3719" data-end=3D"3758" class=3D"">4. Cl=C3=A9s Primaires=
 et Cl=C3=A9s =C3=89trang=C3=A8res</h2>
<p data-start=3D"3760" data-end=3D"3887" class=3D"">Les <strong data-start=
=3D"3764" data-end=3D"3782">cl=C3=A9s primaires</strong> et <strong data-st=
art=3D"3786" data-end=3D"3805">cl=C3=A9s =C3=A9trang=C3=A8res</strong> sont=
 essentielles pour l=E2=80=99int=C3=A9grit=C3=A9 des donn=C3=A9es et les re=
lations entre les tables.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"3889" data-end=3D"3905" class=3D"">Cl=C3=A9 primaire</h3>
<p data-start=3D"3907" data-end=3D"4124" class=3D"">Une <strong data-start=
=3D"3911" data-end=3D"3927">cl=C3=A9 primaire</strong> est un champ ou un e=
nsemble de champs qui identifie de mani=C3=A8re unique chaque ligne d'une t=
able. Aucune valeur dans une colonne de cl=C3=A9 primaire ne peut =C3=AAtre=
 nulle et chaque valeur doit =C3=AAtre unique.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"4126" data-end=3D"4140" class=3D"">Exemple :</h4>
<p data-start=3D"4142" data-end=3D"4260" class=3D"">Dans la table <code dat=
a-start=3D"4156" data-end=3D"4166">Employ=C3=A9s</code>, le champ <code dat=
a-start=3D"4177" data-end=3D"4189">id_employ=C3=A9</code> peut =C3=AAtre un=
e cl=C3=A9 primaire car chaque employ=C3=A9 a un identifiant unique.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"4262" data-end=3D"4279" class=3D"">Cl=C3=A9 =C3=A9trang=
=C3=A8re</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4281" data-end=3D"4467" class=3D"">Une <strong data-start=
=3D"4285" data-end=3D"4302">cl=C3=A9 =C3=A9trang=C3=A8re</strong> est un ch=
amp dans une table qui =C3=A9tablit une relation avec une cl=C3=A9 primaire=
 dans une autre table. Elle permet de lier les enregistrements de deux tabl=
es diff=C3=A9rentes.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"4469" data-end=3D"4483" class=3D"">Exemple :</h4>
<p data-start=3D"4485" data-end=3D"4516" class=3D"">Imaginons une table <co=
de data-start=3D"4505" data-end=3D"4514">Projets</code> :</p>
<div class=3D"overflow-x-auto contain-inline-size"><table data-start=3D"451=
8" data-end=3D"4689" node=3D"[object Object]"><thead data-start=3D"4518" da=
ta-end=3D"4560"><tr data-start=3D"4518" data-end=3D"4560"><th data-start=3D=
"4518" data-end=3D"4530">id_projet</th><th data-start=3D"4530" data-end=3D"=
4546">nom_projet</th><th data-start=3D"4546" data-end=3D"4560">id_employ=C3=
=A9</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start=3D"4604" data-end=3D"4689"><tr data-=
start=3D"4604" data-end=3D"4646"><td>1</td><td>Projet A</td><td>1</td></tr>=
<tr data-start=3D"4647" data-end=3D"4689"><td>2</td><td>Projet B</td><td>2<=
/td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p data-start=3D"4691" data-end=3D"4827" class=3D"">Dans cet exemple, <code=
 data-start=3D"4709" data-end=3D"4721">id_employ=C3=A9</code> dans la table=
 <code data-start=3D"4736" data-end=3D"4745">Projets</code> est une cl=C3=
=A9 =C3=A9trang=C3=A8re qui fait r=C3=A9f=C3=A9rence =C3=A0 <code data-star=
t=3D"4789" data-end=3D"4801">id_employ=C3=A9</code> dans la table <code dat=
a-start=3D"4816" data-end=3D"4826">Employ=C3=A9s</code>.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"4829" data-end=3D"4832" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"4834" data-end=3D"4866" class=3D"">5. Les Relations Entre=
 Tables</h2>
<p data-start=3D"4868" data-end=3D"5009" class=3D"">Les bases de donn=C3=A9=
es relationnelles permettent de d=C3=A9finir des <strong data-start=3D"4930=
" data-end=3D"4943">relations</strong> entre les tables. Il existe trois ty=
pes principaux de relations :</p>
<ol data-start=3D"5011" data-end=3D"5326">
<li data-start=3D"5011" data-end=3D"5101" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5014" data-end=3D"5101" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
014" data-end=3D"5031">Un-=C3=A0-un (1:1)</strong> : Une ligne d=E2=80=99un=
e table est li=C3=A9e =C3=A0 une seule ligne d=E2=80=99une autre table.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5102" data-end=3D"5200" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5105" data-end=3D"5200" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
105" data-end=3D"5129">Un-=C3=A0-plusieurs (1:N)</strong> : Une ligne d=E2=
=80=99une table est li=C3=A9e =C3=A0 plusieurs lignes d=E2=80=99une autre t=
able.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5201" data-end=3D"5326" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5204" data-end=3D"5326" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
204" data-end=3D"5235">Plusieurs-=C3=A0-plusieurs (N:M)</strong> : Plusieur=
s lignes dans une table peuvent =C3=AAtre li=C3=A9es =C3=A0 plusieurs ligne=
s d=E2=80=99une autre table.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start=3D"5328" data-end=3D"5469" class=3D"">Exemple de relation <st=
rong data-start=3D"5348" data-end=3D"5366">Un-=C3=A0-plusieurs</strong> : U=
n employ=C3=A9 peut travailler sur plusieurs projets, mais chaque projet es=
t attribu=C3=A9 =C3=A0 un seul employ=C3=A9.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"5471" data-end=3D"5474" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"5476" data-end=3D"5516" class=3D"">6. Normalisation des B=
ases de Donn=C3=A9es</h2>
<p data-start=3D"5518" data-end=3D"5787" class=3D"">La <strong data-start=
=3D"5521" data-end=3D"5538">normalisation</strong> est le processus d'organ=
isation des donn=C3=A9es dans la base de donn=C3=A9es pour minimiser la red=
ondance et am=C3=A9liorer l'int=C3=A9grit=C3=A9 des donn=C3=A9es. Il existe=
 plusieurs formes normales (1NF, 2NF, 3NF, etc.) qui visent =C3=A0 structur=
er les donn=C3=A9es de mani=C3=A8re logique.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"5789" data-end=3D"5824" class=3D"">Objectifs de la normal=
isation :</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"5825" data-end=3D"5988">
<li data-start=3D"5825" data-end=3D"5864" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5827" data-end=3D"5864" class=3D"">Minimiser la duplicatio=
n des donn=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5865" data-end=3D"5936" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5867" data-end=3D"5936" class=3D"">Pr=C3=A9venir les anoma=
lies de mise =C3=A0 jour, de suppression et d'insertion.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5937" data-end=3D"5988" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5939" data-end=3D"5988" class=3D"">Garantir la coh=C3=A9re=
nce et l'int=C3=A9grit=C3=A9 des donn=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"5990" data-end=3D"6223" class=3D"">Exemple : Si une table =
<code data-start=3D"6013" data-end=3D"6024">Commandes</code> contient des i=
nformations sur les produits et les clients, il peut =C3=AAtre plus logique=
 de s=C3=A9parer les informations sur les produits et les clients dans des =
tables distinctes pour =C3=A9viter la redondance.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"6225" data-end=3D"6228" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"6230" data-end=3D"6275" class=3D"">7. Langage SQL (Struct=
ured Query Language)</h2>
<p data-start=3D"6277" data-end=3D"6522" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=
=3D"6280" data-end=3D"6287">SQL</strong> est le langage utilis=C3=A9 pour i=
nteragir avec une base de donn=C3=A9es relationnelle. Il permet de manipule=
r les donn=C3=A9es (insertion, mise =C3=A0 jour, suppression) et de d=C3=A9=
finir la structure des bases de donn=C3=A9es (cr=C3=A9ation, modification d=
e tables).</p>
<p data-start=3D"6524" data-end=3D"6562" class=3D"">Voici quelques commande=
s SQL de base :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6564" data-end=3D"6729">
<li data-start=3D"6564" data-end=3D"6599" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6566" data-end=3D"6599" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"656=
6" data-end=3D"6574">SELECT</code> : R=C3=A9cup=C3=A9rer des donn=C3=A9es.<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6600" data-end=3D"6647" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6602" data-end=3D"6647" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"660=
2" data-end=3D"6615">INSERT INTO</code> : Ajouter de nouvelles donn=C3=A9es=
.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6648" data-end=3D"6693" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6650" data-end=3D"6693" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"665=
0" data-end=3D"6658">UPDATE</code> : Modifier des donn=C3=A9es existantes.<=
/p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6694" data-end=3D"6729" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6696" data-end=3D"6729" class=3D""><code data-start=3D"669=
6" data-end=3D"6704">DELETE</code> : Supprimer des donn=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6731" data-end=3D"6734" class=3D"">
