2250" data-end=3D"2260">MySQLi</strong> :</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2264" data-end=3D"2439">
<li data-start=3D"2264" data-end=3D"2439" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2266" data-end=3D"2439" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
266" data-end=3D"2295">Supporte uniquement MySQL</strong>. MySQLi est une e=
xtension sp=C3=A9cifique =C3=A0 MySQL, ce qui signifie que vous ne pouvez l=
'utiliser que pour interagir avec des bases de donn=C3=A9es MySQL.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"2441" data-end=3D"2454" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2445" data-end=3D"2452">PDO</strong> :</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2455" data-end=3D"2706">
<li data-start=3D"2455" data-end=3D"2706" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"2457" data-end=3D"2706" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
457" data-end=3D"2496">Supporte plusieurs bases de donn=C3=A9es</strong>. P=
DO est plus flexible que MySQLi car il permet de se connecter =C3=A0 une va=
ri=C3=A9t=C3=A9 de bases de donn=C3=A9es, y compris <strong data-start=3D"2=
606" data-end=3D"2615">MySQL</strong>, <strong data-start=3D"2617" data-end=
=3D"2631">PostgreSQL</strong>, <strong data-start=3D"2633" data-end=3D"2643=
">SQLite</strong>, <strong data-start=3D"2645" data-end=3D"2654">MSSQL</str=
ong>, <strong data-start=3D"2656" data-end=3D"2666">Oracle</strong>, et d=
=E2=80=99autres, en utilisant la m=C3=AAme API.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"2708" data-end=3D"2889" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"2=
708" data-end=3D"2722">Conclusion</strong> : Si vous devez interagir avec p=
lusieurs types de bases de donn=C3=A9es, <strong data-start=3D"2791" data-e=
nd=3D"2798">PDO</strong> est un meilleur choix. Si vous travaillez uniqueme=
nt avec MySQL, <strong data-start=3D"2864" data-end=3D"2874">MySQLi</strong=
> est suffisant.</p>
