xception est lev=C3=A9e et captur=C3=A9e. L'objet <code data-start=3D"3494"=
 data-end=3D"3505">Exception</code> contient des informations utiles qui pe=
uvent =C3=AAtre extraites gr=C3=A2ce =C3=A0 des m=C3=A9thodes telles que <c=
ode data-start=3D"3598" data-end=3D"3612">getMessage()</code>, <code data-s=
tart=3D"3614" data-end=3D"3625">getCode()</code>, <code data-start=3D"3627"=
 data-end=3D"3638">getFile()</code>, et <code data-start=3D"3643" data-end=
=3D"3654">getLine()</code>.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"3657" data-end=3D"3660" class=3D"">
<h2 data-start=3D"3662" data-end=3D"3709" class=3D"">4. Utilisation de <cod=
e data-start=3D"3683" data-end=3D"3688">try</code>, <code data-start=3D"369=
0" data-end=3D"3697">catch</code>, et <code data-start=3D"3702" data-end=3D=
"3709">throw</code></h2>
<p data-start=3D"3711" data-end=3D"3939" class=3D"">Les exceptions sont lev=
=C3=A9es =C3=A0 l=E2=80=99aide de l=E2=80=99instruction <code data-start=3D=
"3764" data-end=3D"3771">throw</code>. Vous pouvez ensuite les capturer ave=
c une structure <code data-start=3D"3825" data-end=3D"3830">try</code>...<c=
ode data-start=3D"3833" data-end=3D"3840">catch</code>, qui permet d=E2=80=
=99isoler le code susceptible de provoquer une exception et de le traiter c=
orrectement.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"3941" data-end=3D"3970" class=3D"">4.1 L=E2=80=99instruct=
ion <code data-start=3D"3963" data-end=3D"3970">throw</code></h3>
<p data-start=3D"3972" data-end=3D"4146" class=3D"">L'instruction <code dat=
a-start=3D"3986" data-end=3D"3993">throw</code> permet de lancer une except=
ion. Elle prend comme argument une instance de la classe <code data-start=
=3D"4078" data-end=3D"4089">Exception</code> ou d=E2=80=99une classe person=
nalis=C3=A9e qui h=C3=A9rite de <code data-start=3D"4134" data-end=3D"4145"=
>Exception</code>.</p>
